        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Compare a repository Business Template with its installed ERP5/ZODB representation.\n
\n
READ-ONLY. Reports changes made only in the repository, only in ERP5, and on both sides\n
(conflicts), plus Python/XML validation failures, and whether updating ERP5 from the\n
repository and exporting ERP5 to the repository are safe.\n
\n
The three states compared are: the baseline (the git HEAD commit of the shared working\n
copy), the current repository files (working tree), and the current installed ZODB\n
representation (exported to a temporary directory).\n
\n
REQUIRED ERP5 and repository side share the working copy configured in\n
default_configurator_preference (my_preferred_working_copy_list).\n
\n
Scoping (drift checks on big templates): pass path_pattern (glob, \'*\' spans \'/\',\n
matched against repository-root-relative paths like bt5/erp5_core/CatalogMethodTemplateItem/...)\n
to compare only the matching paths — e.g. a scoped status on \'*supply_line*\'\n
answers "is my catalog method in drift?" in seconds on a 1000+-file BT.\n
summary_only=true / max_list=N cap the returned lists (counts and \'_more\'\n
markers say what was left out); with no explicit summary_only, templates with\n
more than 500 files are summarized automatically, because a full per-file\n
sweep on them is what used to time this tool out.\n
\n
Returns JSON with: business_template, file_count, repository_to_zodb\n
(modified/added/deleted with *_count), zodb_to_repository, conflicts,\n
validation, update_from_repository_safe, export_to_repository_safe, and a\n
summary_note when the summary was set automatically.\n
</string> </value>
